## 3.1 The central narrative experience

Chapter 9 begins with an ordinary reason for Ira to move through Kuoh.

The city becomes an adventure.

An ordinary act of helping someone leads him beyond the familiar environment.

He unknowingly crosses into an astral environment, becomes the subject of a malicious presence's attention, and reaches an isolated house where he encounters an inexplicable purple phenomenon.

A structural failure puts him in immediate danger. A one-tooth necklace is pulled free during the fall. Ira escapes the immediate structure.

The chapter ends with the purple phenomenon reflected in his eyes.

This is the governing movement:

**Ordinary life → urban exploration → human interruption → pursuit → environmental unreliability → stalking → isolation → perceptual rupture → physical collapse → escape → unresolved visual consequence.**

